deluge-nextdrive changelog
==========================


v1.1.0
------
+ Optional completed path per location: finished downloads are moved to a folder on the drive they were downloaded to.
+ The completed path is kept when a label is set after the torrent was added, and across restarts.
+ A magnet placed on another drive is now still moved to its move-completed path when it finishes (Deluge turns that off after any storage move).
+ Labels whose move-completed path is under the first location's completed path no longer stop a torrent from being placed.


v1.0.0
------
+ Basic functionality.
+ Default reserve is now 5 GiB.
+ Magnets waiting for metadata stay on hold across a daemon restart.
+ A resumed paused magnet is no longer paused again once its metadata arrives.
+ Space being filled by torrents added a moment ago is now counted, so a burst of adds no longer overfills a drive.
+ Magnets being moved to another drive are counted on the drive they are moving to.
+ Data already on any listed drive is reused instead of downloaded again.
+ Bad settings (relative paths, inf/nan or text reserves, bad labels, "false" as text) are rejected and nothing is changed.
+ Setting errors are shown in the Web UI instead of hanging it.
+ Clicking Apply in Preferences without opening the NextDrive page no longer clears the drive list.
+ Old or damaged config files are repaired on start instead of breaking magnet adds.
+ A NextDrive error can no longer stop a torrent from being added.
